In `parse_ipv6()`, when parsing an IPv6 address string with a port number (e.g., `[<ipv6_addr>]:<port>`), the function extracts the port string following `]:`.
At lines 780-793:
```c
len = str_len - end - 1 - 2;
ptr += 2;
for (i = 0; i < len; i++) {
    if (!ptr[i]) {
        len = i;
        break;
    }
}
memcpy(ipaddr, ptr, len);
ipaddr[len] = '\0';
