However, `rxMsg.data` is defined in `CO_driver_target.h` as a fixed-size buffer of 8 bytes (`uint8_t data[8]`). In Zephyr, CAN frames can have a payload length (`frame->dlc`) greater than 8 bytes (such as in CAN FD mode where `frame->dlc` can be up to 64 bytes, or if a frame with DLC > 8 is received on the CAN bus). 

