Invoke `eeprom_write(dev, -4, payload, 4)`. `(-4 + 4)` wraps to `0 <= dev_config->size`, passing validation. The driver then executes `memcpy(dev_config->rambuf - 4, payload, 4)`, corrupting memory immediately preceding `rambuf`.

